{"base_rate":0.16890080428954424,"brier":0.07257788203753351,"bss":0.48296527649769583,"bss_hi":0.5770325693133282,"bss_lo":0.36741468837845226,"chart":{"base":[281.0,50.3],"fp":[218.3,308.9],"lead":"62,213.7 272,205 482,173.4 692,143.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.48 — higher than 89% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end +14pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.5 °C — better than 17% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 75% → rained 66%"},"rel":"62,462 121.5,409.7 536.4,178.9"},"country":"ES","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.03156836461126006,"ess":290.5139152804179,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Malaga</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Malaga rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 746 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMALAGA AEROPUERTO, 8.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.48, ranked 24 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(7&ndash;69) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>433</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>54%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Malaga</b> <span class=\"muted\">Spain</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.48</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>7&ndash;69\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>746 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Malaga &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Malaga\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.452,352.0235294117647 113.80157894736843,295.7894736842105 248.63378378378377,150.81081081081084 396.6146153846154,22.66666666666663 396.6146153846154,50.666666666666686 248.63378378378377,224.59459459459458 113.80157894736843,353.2631578947368 71.452,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"320.5201072386059\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"320.5201072386059\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,378.6374133949192 71.452,360.5882352941176 113.80157894736843,305.36842105263156 248.63378378378377,185.24324324324323 396.6146153846154,97.33333333333331\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 433 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"378.6374133949192\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.452\" cy=\"360.5882352941176\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 16%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"113.80157894736843\" cy=\"305.36842105263156\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 54% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"248.63378378378377\" cy=\"185.24324324324323\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.6146153846154\" cy=\"97.33333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Malaga the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.54) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.28).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>183</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>-0.279</td><td class='num'>1.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.387</td><td class='num'>4.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.487</td><td class='num'>7.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>211</td><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'>0.539</td><td class='num'>3.5%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":36.72016,"lon":-4.42034,"n":746,"n_cities":213,"name":"Malaga","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":433,"obs":0.009237875288683603,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03799999999999999,"n":85,"obs":0.058823529411764705,"sig":false},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.15763157894736843,"n":76,"obs":0.21052631578947367,"sig":false},{"hi":0.83,"lo":0.3,"mean":0.5385135135135135,"n":74,"obs":0.5405405405405406,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.83,"mean":0.9565384615384616,"n":78,"obs":0.782051282051282,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.5,"provisional":false,"rank":24,"rank_hi":69.0,"rank_lo":7.0,"reliability":0.0035677219265326924,"resolution":0.06936292049210777,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"malaga","station":"MALAGA AEROPUERTO","timezone":"Europe/Madrid"}